All Lojban words beginning with a vowel are supposed to have "." prepended,
however, they are not /required/ in text as long as the word boundaries are
clearly defined.

It is assumed that in such cases the reader knows that the pause normally
indicated by "." is implicitly there, so in practice, many jbopre don't
write it, either because of aesthetics, laziness, or possibly other reasons.

For example, {coi djeims mi e do klama lo vecnu} is the same as {coi.djeims.
mi .e do klama lo vecnu}.

Personally, I feel that omitting /any/
"." is a bad practice that is potentially confusing, especially to newbies,
so I endeavor not to do so.

to pu benji di'u fo lo mi me la.android. fonxa toi

mu'o mi'e.aionys.

